# #5851 widened catch-up (a5e2e2ef, #5851 comment 6668868649): the catch-up is a true replay
# to max(reported bound, close head - 1) on the tick. C's Replay, which reads one durable entry at
# a time to any target, is every such catch-up; these mutations break W1-W3.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestCatchUpCheckpointPastRead
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
PERTURBS: Replay
SUMMARY: the catch-up sets the checkpoint to its target rather than to the contiguous position it read (W1), passing another author's allocated offset not yet durable (a stale donor's write), which L never applies once it lands
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 0, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ rp[a] + 1 \in durable
    /\ rp[a] + 1 >= floor
    /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![a] = @ \cup {rp[a] + 1}]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the checkpoint moves to the target past an offset not yet read.
    /\ rp[a] + 1 < next
    /\ rp[a] + 1 >= floor
    /\ cache' = IF rp[a] + 1 \in durable THEN [cache EXCEPT ![a] = @ \cup {rp[a] + 1}] ELSE cache
--- END
